2025-09-24 Shivam Patel <shivamp12@hotmail.com>
		* I need to figure out a way to possibly speed up build time if possible cause I'm losing too much time on it.
		* Fixed the tmp-emit-10.cc build error and large immediate handling in prologue and epilogue:
			- I ditched the fallback patterns (add_fallback<mode>3, sub_fallback<mode>3) from etca.md that were 
			  causing gen_reg_rtx() calls during prologue and epilogue expansion (not allowed at that stage?)
			- Updated expand_prologue() and expand_epilogue() in etca.cc to handle large immediates 
			  directly by splitting them into: load immediate into temp register (ETCA_R8/t0) + arithmetic
			- For small immediates (-16 to 15): uses direct gen_subhi3/gen_addhi3 as before
			- For large immediates: uses movhi + subhi3/addhi3 with temp register to avoid predicate violations
			- I believe I fixed missing ret instruction issue by using emit_jump_insn(gen_returner()) instead of emit_insn(),
				also added new pattern in etca.md for return & simple_return. Created function etca_can_use_simple_return_p which
				checks 
		* Current problem is with nested loops failing for some reason.

